flames pour from an apartment in the  twin parks complex pictures shared on  the citizen app revealing the first  moments of what's become one of the  deadliest residential fires in modern  american history  in the three minutes it took fire crews  to reach the building they said the  smoke had reached every floor  they found victims on each one survivors  among them people who knew children who  died describe the horror and the  helplessness tomorrow is a school day  they're going to ask me why they are  friends  they're going to ask me tomorrow where  they are friends because then go  together then come back together what  i'm going to tell them tomorrow  the windows were blown out either by the  heat of the fire or residents desperate  for air smashing them it was a horrific  scene because you have to realize  besides being a firefighter you have to  deal with the mental stress of seeing  this carnage of what happened in the  bronx today  within hours investigators had  pinpointed the cause this fire began in  an apartment that spans two floors on  the second and third floor of the  building  it started in a malfunctioning electric  space heater  and because doors to that apartment and  a stairwell had been left open the fire  spread quickly with no external fire  escape the only way out was those  stairwells filled with smoke  we are indeed a city in shock  it's impossible to go into that room  where scorers of family  who are in such grief who are in pain  to see it in a mother's eyes as i held  her  who lost her entire family  it all happened days after 12 people  including eight children were killed in  a fire in a house in philadelphia its  thought smoke detectors there weren't  working  at the twin parks one resident said he'd  ignored the smoke alarm at first because  there have been so many false alarms  recently he soon realized like so many  that this one was horribly real greg  milam sky news
 

